Intelligent Video Surveillance System (MVP) - Project Approach
-------------------------------------------------------------

1. Overview
-----------
We are building a minimal viable product (MVP) for an intelligent video surveillance system.
The system will run on a laptop using its webcam for live footage and a web application
for user interaction. Core features include:
- Secure login
- Real-time alerts (new face detected, weapon detection)
- Automated attendance logging

2. Tech Stack (Minimal Version)
-------------------------------
Frontend:
- HTML, CSS, JavaScript
- Bootstrap for quick styling
- Basic JS pop-ups for alerts
- Video feed embedded via <video> tag or MJPEG stream

Backend:
- Flask (Python) as the web server
- REST API endpoints for login, attendance, alerts
- Flask-SocketIO for real-time alert push

Computer Vision / ML:
- OpenCV for webcam capture and preprocessing
- Face recognition using pretrained models (Dlib / FaceNet)
- Weapon detection using YOLOv5-small or SSD MobileNet
- Inference runs locally on laptop CPU/GPU

Database:
- SQLite (lightweight, file-based)
- Stores user credentials (hashed), face embeddings, attendance logs, alert logs

Authentication:
- Flask-Login or simple session management
- Password hashing with bcrypt
- Basic role separation (admin vs reviewer)

Deployment:
- Local deployment on laptop (backend + frontend served by Flask)
- No Docker/Cloud required for MVP
- Single process handles webcam, inference, and web app

3. Workflow
-----------
1. User logs into web app (login page).
2. Dashboard displays live webcam feed.
3. Backend runs detection pipeline:
   - Face recognition → attendance marked if known.
   - Weapon detection → alert triggered if confidence > threshold.
4. Alerts pushed to frontend via WebSocket → pop-up notification.
5. Logs stored in SQLite for later review.

4. Next Steps
-------------
- Define folder structure (app.py, static/, templates/, models/, database.db).
- Implement login and dashboard pages.
- Integrate OpenCV with Flask for webcam feed.
- Connect detection pipeline to alert manager.
- Test attendance logging and alert notifications.
- Prepare demo-ready MVP for collaborators to review.

